L	BlindWolf	A blind predator that hunts by sound and smell and spits acid.
L	Brute	Jiralhanae. Huge, strong and quick to anger, the Brutes rose to replace the Elites as the Covenant's enforcers. They wear armor that can be knocked from their heads, and when their pack dies around them they discard their guns and charge on all fours.
L	BruteCaptain	A Brute officer whose hologram banner marks it as a pack leader.
L	BruteChieftain	The leader of a Brute pack, with a gravity hammer that shakes the ground at every blow. It leaps at its targets from a distance.
L	BruteHonorGuard	Brutes in red ceremonial armor, who took the Honor Guard's duties from the Sangheili.
L	BruteStalker	A Brute hunter wearing an active camouflage harness, stalking prey with a Spiker.
L	Drinol	A massive beast from the Covenant's menageries, set loose on the battlefield.
L	Drone	Yanme'e. Insectoid swarms with plasma pistols and needlers, darting through the air, clinging to walls and diving in from above. Individually fragile, dangerous in numbers.
L	DroneCaptain	A red-plated swarm leader. Captains fly under an energy shield and often carry plasma rifles.
L	DroneCaptainMajor	The swarm's senior officer, plated in gold, with a stronger shield than a Captain's.
L	DroneMajor	A seasoned Yanme'e, its carapace plates marked in blue. Tougher than the swarm around it.
L	DroneUltra	A veteran of the swarm in white-plated chitin, able to take far more punishment than its hive-mates.
L	Elite	Sangheili. The Covenant's warrior caste and its field officers: tall, fast, and protected by a recharging energy shield. They command the lesser races, roll out of grenade blasts, and fall back to let their shields return before pressing again. Their armor color tells their rank.
L	EliteCommander	A gold-armored Commander, veteran of many campaigns. Commanders lead from the front and favor the energy sword.
L	EliteHonorGuard	The High Council's ceremonial guard, chosen from the Sangheili's finest and armored in crimson and gold. They guard the Prophets themselves, and the sword is their weapon of choice.
L	EliteMajor	A red-armored Major. Stronger shields than a Minor, better aim, and a commander's habit of directing the Grunts around it.
L	EliteMinor	The blue-armored Minor Domo, the lowest Elite rank and still the most dangerous soldier in most Covenant squads.
L	EliteRanger	Sangheili trained to fight in vacuum and on hostile ground, sealed in an EVA suit and carried by a jump pack. Rangers take the high ground in a fight and drift down onto you from above.
L	EliteRifle	Sangheili armed with long Covenant carbines and pulse carbines, fighting at a distance most Elites would scorn.
L	EliteSpecops	Spec Ops Elites: picked warriors with stronger shields and better weapons, assigned to the operations that matter. They work alongside the Spec Ops Grunts.
L	EliteZealot	A Zealot: a Sangheili of the Covenant's most devout order, sent where the faith's interests are greatest. Expect overwhelming shields and an energy sword.
L	Engineer	Huragok. Living machines of the Forerunners, enslaved by the Covenant to repair and maintain their technology. An Engineer will shield its allies; in this war, it may also be wired to explode.
L	H2Jackal	Kig-Yar as the Covenant fielded them in the war's later years: rifles and carbines instead of pistols, and marksmen who prefer to fight from far away. Expect the long-range ones to keep their distance and their heads down.
L	Jackal	Kig-Yar. Raiders and mercenaries with the keenest eyes in the Covenant, fighting behind a wrist-mounted energy shield. The shield is overcharged plasma's natural prey; otherwise, wait for the gap when it fires and shoot past the edge.
L	JackalMajorHelmet	A Kig-Yar major in the old plated helmet of the first war's pirate captains, carrying a plasma rifle behind a pink point-defence shield. Tougher than the bare-headed ranks; aim for the gun hand when it peeks round the shield's edge.
L	JackalMarksman	A Kig-Yar marksman in the sniper's lensed helmet, trading the beam rifle for a carbine and a faster rate of fire. It keeps its distance and leaves the shield behind.
L	JackalSniper	A Kig-Yar marksman with a beam rifle, in a sealed sniper helmet whose lenses glow in the dark. You will rarely see one before its shot; the pink tracer of the first miss, or those two points of light on the high ground, are the warning.
L	JackalZealot	A Kig-Yar fanatic in gold, armed with a Brute Spiker. Rare, aggressive and unwilling to retreat.
L	SlugMan	A crude, enormous creature of the Covenant's fringes. Slow but hard to kill.
L	ThornBeast	A spined beast that fires quills from its back.
